From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: Support the NVIDIA Tegra video input

The tegra-video driver captures raw Bayer frames from CSI sensors on
Tegra210 without an ISP, so the frames go through the software ISP.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -265,6 +265,7 @@ static const SimplePipelineInfo supportedDevices[] = {
 	{ "mxc-isi", {}, false },
 	{ "qcom-camss", {}, true },
 	{ "sun6i-csi", {}, false },
+	{ "tegra-video", {}, true },
 };
 
 bool isRaw(const StreamConfiguration &cfg)
